    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d341">

                <pb facs="0578" n="552" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v16/pg552"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">396.1 GE/4–2454: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bohlen</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Department
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">official use
                            only<lb/>priority</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-04-24T16:00:00+03:00">April 24, 1954—4 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1313. Repeated information priority Paris 282, priority Geneva 8. Embtel 1304,
                    repeated information Paris 279, Geneva 7, April 23.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d341-f1"/></p>
                <p>Soviets have sent us following reply to note given them yesterday re Geneva
                    conference.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“In connection with note Government United States of America 23 April<anchor
                            n="2" xml:id="d341-f2"/> Government of USSR considers it necessary to
                        state it confirms its position on question of composition Geneva conference
                        as set forth in note April 20.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d341-f3"/></p>
                    <p>With reference to invitations interested states to participate in discussion
                        problem re-establishing peace in Indochina, it goes without saying that this
                        question is matter for consideration of representatives those states whose
                        participation on basis equality is directly provided for in Berlin
                        communiqué”.</p></quote>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bohlen</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
